# $name

A Policy Trace Lab task pack: a cart on a one-dimensional rail. It must stop at the goal
(0.4 m) and keep away from a virtual wall further along the rail. The simulator is about
sixty lines of Python in `$module/simulator.py`, so everything here runs offline with no
assets. Use it as a template for your own simulator.

| Policy | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `$name/steady` | Commands the goal directly; stops at the goal and stays clear of the wall. |
| `$name/eager` | Commands far beyond the goal; reaches it, but overshoots toward the wall. |
| `$name/slow` | Commands a tiny step; never reaches the goal within 200 steps. |

Conditions: `nominal` (wall at 0.55 m) and `close_wall` (wall at 0.48 m).

## Install and check

Run these from this directory, in an environment where `guided-streaming-policy` is installed.

```bash
pip install .
gsp lab tasks list
gsp lab tasks check $name
gsp lab demo --task $name --out out/demo
```

`gsp lab tasks check` runs the conformance kit: the contract version, the schemas on a
recorded sample, the ten fixture cases, pins, and a same-seed reset fingerprint check. The
demo exits 1 by design: its fixture holds a seeded regression.

## Compare two policies

`configs/comparison.json` compares `$name/steady` with `$name/eager` over seeds 0 to 3;
`configs/gate.json` holds the release rule. Commit both before you look at results.

```bash
gsp lab run --comparison configs/comparison.json --variant baseline --out out/runs/baseline
gsp lab run --comparison configs/comparison.json --variant candidate --out out/runs/candidate
gsp lab doctor out/runs/baseline --out out/doctor-baseline
gsp lab compare out/runs/baseline out/runs/candidate --comparison configs/comparison.json --out out/compare
gsp lab gate out/compare/compare.json --gate configs/gate.json --out out/gate
gsp lab report out/compare/compare.json --gate out/gate/gate.json --out out/report
```

The gate exits 1: `$name/eager` reaches the goal, so native success holds, but it comes
closer to the wall than the 0.1 m threshold. Open `out/report/report.html` to replay it.

## Make it your own

1. Replace the simulator in `$module/simulator.py` and the run hook in `$module/adapter.py`.
2. Keep `probe()` and `policies()` free of heavy imports: use `importlib.util.find_spec`.
3. Regenerate the fixtures and pins with `python tools/build_fixtures.py`, then run
   `python -m unittest discover -s tests` and `gsp lab tasks check $name`.

The contract is described in "Adding a simulator" in the Policy Trace Lab documentation.
